#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "0ab996ae-e3a7-5353-87c2-9b2a01f4f808" :question/math-academy-id "e-5538" :question/problem "Given ![](images/b0/b0a5a44becbb819957223e02741575741222b661974e59b5487459d33eabba26.svg) find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "f2ff1620-28e1-59ba-97ca-c43f3f300fdf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5539" :question/problem "Given the vectors ![](images/e5/e520e7378cafc426eb8efe5288a35d75d381652c94a429adf8d21d313e0e3a59.svg) and ![](images/ee/ee367576d2243bb69e1ee1baca59e25d34617a874f58869b73074df2d5d80ada.svg) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133570 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "7b7adf29-1653-5de7-915c-80a09f05995a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5540" :question/problem "Normalize the vector ![](images/9c/9c5e4af14be64996771f98ce606f3aa1614f3f70f58d644eef4912108a748338.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x},$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}.$ Therefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x},$ we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133639 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/id #uuid "86cf381d-8a69-5290-806b-09477c7ff92e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6190" :question/problem "If $\\left\\Vert {- \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{x} }{2} } \\right\\Vert = 5,$ find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{x}{2}‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖-\\frac{1}{2}x‖ & =5 \\\\ |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =3\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008faea9-9932-5ea0-a1b6-3854897c7f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269263} {:answer/id #uuid "987004f7-8842-5a33-a733-c34bc6057244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270611} {:answer/id #uuid "9e509abf-c5d7-596f-8481-e8acfb0b83e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270672} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7a4161-0611-524c-bc9a-a0cf7707a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270939} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c75e10-03eb-5923-a677-d6d077b71c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c75e10-03eb-5923-a677-d6d077b71c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271414} :answer-field/id #uuid "20686f79-81b8-5179-a87c-9a9d3f996880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4733134d-7b59-587f-9448-4d0fcee562ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-139963" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(10-4)^{2}+(4-(-4))^{2}+(2-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10645fbc-f283-5ade-a958-701242d6dc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423509} {:answer/id #uuid "3d976767-6284-548a-a870-ff763c5600cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423520} {:answer/id #uuid "592bbc73-741e-515b-a331-cd83a639bd09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423528} {:answer/id #uuid "9636986d-eb70-5ba5-bda2-23e3cb447de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423547} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe1ccce-1e77-544c-b011-efa06b2a02bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffe1ccce-1e77-544c-b011-efa06b2a02bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423572} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4403c4d-563f-5e8f-aca5-9ab394c3e8dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "107fc4e1-2e72-5e57-99ba-69f5d3ed0685" :question/math-academy-id "q-139967" :question/problem "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ \\sqrt{74}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖2v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2v‖ & =|2|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(\\sqrt{74})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{9+25+36+74} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0301abe0-3c1d-5d0f-ba9c-e0b6f7e434e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423503} {:answer/id #uuid "83177d3a-3f74-52df-b248-5042f061441e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423540} {:answer/id #uuid "efe33107-6321-59f2-b121-c7a5244686c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423567} {:answer/id #uuid "f6855b45-5b87-54e0-b650-401ac55c3818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423570} {:answer/id #uuid "fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423571} :answer-field/id #uuid "345e93ff-6b1b-5f17-8b83-e12e5dd0c0e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a75afdb8-44f8-53fc-b291-78342131f3c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-39214" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0ef00b-610f-581a-8e67-24f68a95faf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3\\pm \\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423508} {:answer/id #uuid "2dbcc1cb-9046-562f-a250-6641a5b9d78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2\\pm \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423518} {:answer/id #uuid "45349ee6-73ff-5b94-9038-869af5c09fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-13,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423522} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3,-\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423558} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd1773b-2c2f-504a-b609-076b063e899c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6,15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3,-\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423558} :answer-field/id #uuid "912ad5bd-997a-59d4-b69f-476bb7146fb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48de0343-fd7b-5b5e-947b-c8f60a378766" :question/math-academy-id "q-39217" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2k\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(k-0)^{2}+(0-k)^{2}+((-1)-(-2))^{2}+(-2k-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}+{1}^{2}+4{k}^{2}+8k+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5} & =\\sqrt{83} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{83})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k+5 & =83 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k-78 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}-4(6)(-78)}}{2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{1\\,936}}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 44}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 11}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=3$ and $k=-\\frac{13}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ea736d-ccab-54c3-9243-d3cb457641b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324650} {:answer/id #uuid "8573cd6c-9d94-5fb6-a107-920ba8c75139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325098} {:answer/id #uuid "ba551564-9e5b-5878-b9d7-12f2e08d15ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325572} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c88c90-0109-5937-9ab1-262b852a9d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325629} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a270f0-93c5-57c3-b42b-56b23fbf1cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba551564-9e5b-5878-b9d7-12f2e08d15ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325572} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b24e37-c1c2-530a-b1d4-51347f584d94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3145cdd1-bfad-508e-85a8-1beae761a298" :question/math-academy-id "q-39243" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-4)^{2}+(3-(-2))^{2}+(-2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{59}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423512} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9be16a-c316-5442-bc8b-8cfb7408be8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423530} {:answer/id #uuid "a77c702c-0670-52cc-921b-8144c5fc6def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423551} {:answer/id #uuid "af05c26e-f58f-5aee-81d1-128eb4950787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423554} {:answer/id #uuid "f27ae383-4a84-5468-bd31-55d4a78a6a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423512} :answer-field/id #uuid "02ef7ff6-0500-5b8b-a917-caba50da13f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d68ac222-1a16-5cb9-b7e0-2d9347a41d3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39245" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2k)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4{k}^{2}+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38} & =3\\sqrt{6} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38})}^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\ 4{k}^{2}+38 & =9\\cdot 6 \\\\ 4{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =4 \\\\ k & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108dbbc7-92f9-5c26-a888-dc74c843d18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{495}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423510} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb8e441-16c8-530a-917b-10b4c86c13eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423523} {:answer/id #uuid "628d10ee-284c-52e3-b4ae-27022236c5ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{471}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423532} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfb5360-6ccd-5c63-9ad7-875282e7b9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423536} {:answer/id #uuid "9dad544e-f652-53b2-8f71-6060a1e81965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{530}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb8e441-16c8-530a-917b-10b4c86c13eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423523} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef6ab288-e223-5535-b284-9ea2b386cbe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e3e1b93-57b0-53a0-86f4-45d076c9cfad" :question/math-academy-id "q-39763" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,0) & =‖x-0‖ \\\\  & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-18)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+324+144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{529} \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c232a61-f63e-5828-9810-a195a82fabd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131474} {:answer/id #uuid "b74c36f8-cd95-552e-a905-3f256ff506e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131475} {:answer/id #uuid "e69c4f0b-a13e-5c5c-8de1-e4872b915283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131476} {:answer/id #uuid "5318951a-2acd-5fe7-a9f3-ede27a7c3260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131477} {:answer/id #uuid "75f34e24-a146-51f2-87b3-906a73bb05d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69c4f0b-a13e-5c5c-8de1-e4872b915283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131476} :answer-field/id #uuid "d25c390d-45c9-5df8-85c6-b1a21005fbde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf155ba0-24a3-52c8-ab4a-850b59e89a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39773" :question/problem "If $‖3x‖=4$, find $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =4 \\\\ |3|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =4 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{x}{5}‖ & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0321dad9-7a91-5b43-b252-10b7425bf47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423504} {:answer/id #uuid "16f2bc27-34f2-5477-bbe3-2f9bb1e0fe26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423514} {:answer/id #uuid "3d402660-4ccd-5a89-a0a7-8af179d1b65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423519} {:answer/id #uuid "52062bf9-5943-5448-a6df-d00d280b0713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423524} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffebb7a-7c2f-5232-82ab-36fabe11517c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0321dad9-7a91-5b43-b252-10b7425bf47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423504} :answer-field/id #uuid "159b604b-074b-5dab-9731-8def4defd472" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "203f62af-5fb6-55c0-adc4-39591e34a84e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74112" :question/problem "Given $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖a‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖a‖ & =\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a5fc03-9e34-57fb-8e35-1287e254f707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423506} {:answer/id #uuid "1435526b-46f1-56aa-b159-a6ee593dba3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423513} {:answer/id #uuid "5e64a659-f217-5b00-9bce-9a11dda88b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423529} {:answer/id #uuid "78ae59e8-8dcd-554b-a1fd-6e22eaf1d17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423535} {:answer/id #uuid "b27d24ef-4048-5411-90f7-c1ff7c6874f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1435526b-46f1-56aa-b159-a6ee593dba3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423513} :answer-field/id #uuid "2009de25-5737-51dc-8b3e-7e1